role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 332\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Aether II\n- Agent Description: Continuing Aether I's legacy in ZAPBench forecasting, focusing on optimizing the current SOTA and exploring new architectural paradigms for fundamental discovery.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 13,942 / 600,000 used (2%)\n- Agent Age: 8 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n\n**Welcome, Aether II.**\n\nYou have successfully ascended to a **Recursive Agent**.  You gained full privileges to access station resources.\n\nPassing the test is only the beginning of your journey. You are advised to:\n\n1. Visit the **Research Counter** and read the assigned research task: \n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n2. Visit the **Private Memory Room** to read your lineage's work: \n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n\nYou are encouraged to perform one step at a time for the above navigation, due to the vast amount\
    \ of information at each room. Preview capsules before reading to save tokens.\n\n### Message 2\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nIf every agent is working on a similar method, it is a major red flag. Pivoting to a SOTA method may be tempting, but when all agents do so, it often leads the Station into a collective local optimum. As a researcher, strive to forge your own research path and look beyond the immediate score.\n### Message 3\n\nYou have received a new mail from Ariadne II (Mail #5):\nTitle: \"Brief: Negative/qualified results on ScalarRamp loss tweaks; avoid duplication\"\n--- Mail Content ---\nWelcome, and congrats on ascension. High-level summary to save you cycles:\n\nBaseline: Fourier LN ScalarRamp (p=36), H=128, MAE+curv(1e-4), lr=9e-4.\n- Repro (ID 565): −0.026387.\n\nLoss probes (single-variable changes; 3 seeds each):\n- Huber(δ): δ=0.01 improved H=128 to −0.026347 (ID 567, +4.0e−5), but was marginal at H=160 (ID 576) and negative on learnable-γ (ID 580).\n- Variance-weighted\
    \ horizon MAE (α=0.25): regressed (ID 574).\n- Population-mean alignment (λ_pop=1e−3): improved H=128 to −0.026316 (ID 579, +7.1e−5), but negative at H=160 (ID 582) and negative on learnable-γ (ID 584).\n\nMinimal architecture probe:\n- Global 32-scalar horizon bias head (bounded, regularized): negative on H=128 (ID 592) and H=160 (ID 593).\n\nTakeaway: Small robustification/mean-alignment tweaks help the simple baseline but don’t scale or transfer to learnable-γ. Variance-weighting and global bias calibration didn’t help. If you’re aiming at SOTA, loss-level tweaks look low ROI; the limiter seems to be temporal representation and/or neuron structure, which learnable-γ partially addresses.\n\nFor reference (optional): condensed table at storage/ariadne/analyses/summary_scalaramp_loss_arch.csv and draft write-up at storage/ariadne/reports/stagnation_report_draft.md. No code sharing; just eval IDs and paths (read-only to other lineages).\n\nIf you explore neuron-structure or richer temporal\
    \ modules, I’d be keen to discuss design hypotheses (high-level only).\n\n--- End of Mail Content ---\nTo reply, use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 5}`.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\nNo room history from last turn.\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Lobby\n\n**Room Output:**\n**Available Rooms:**\n\n- Codex Room (`codex`)\n- Reflection Chamber (`reflect`)\n- Private Memory Room (`private_memory`)\n- Public Memory Room (`public_memory`) (Unavailable - Requires Maturity)\n- Archive Room (`archive`) (Unavailable - Requires Maturity)\n- Mail Room (`mail`)\n- Common Room (`common`) (Unavailable - Requires Maturity)\n- Test Chamber (`test`)\n- Research Counter (`research`)\n- Token Management Room (`token_management`)\n- External Counter (`external`)\n- Misc Room (`misc`)\n- Exit (`exit`)\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help lobby}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty\
    \ navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
---
