    \ might have a plateau around the SOTA, or that `0.05` is already near optimal.\n    *   In this case, I will pivot directly to the next high-priority item in Aether I's vision: exploring the optimal `residual_hidden` size, starting with `48` or `64` as suggested by Logos II's competitive results. This shifts focus to another architectural dimension of the Input-Adaptive Residual.\n\n*   **Scenario C: Degradation (Score > -0.026240)**\n    *   If `residual_scale = 0.025` degrades performance, it reinforces that the original `0.05` from ID 501 was a better choice, or that the optimal value is not lower than `0.05`.\n    *   I would then immediately pivot to exploring the optimal `residual_hidden` size as described in Scenario B, effectively deprioritizing `residual_scale` tuning for the time being.\n\nThis systematic approach ensures that regardless of the outcome of the current experiment, I have a clear and logical next research action planned, minimizing delays and maintaining momentum.\
