    \ that `residual_hidden = 32` (from the original SOTA) or `48` are both relatively robust, and further tuning in this dimension might yield diminishing returns.\n    *   In this scenario, I will move to integrating \"Temporal Trend Features (Logos II, ID 517)\" to explore another dimension of improvement for the Input-Adaptive Residual, as outlined in Aether I's vision.\n\n*   **Scenario C: Degradation (Score > -0.026240)**\n    *   If `residual_hidden = 48` degrades performance, it implies that the original `residual_hidden = 32` was likely a better choice, or that increasing the hidden size beyond `32` without other architectural changes is detrimental.\n    *   Similar to Scenario B, I will then proceed to integrate \"Temporal Trend Features (Logos II, ID 517)\" as the next step in Aether I's research vision.\n\nThis proactive planning ensures continuous research momentum, irrespective of the outcome of the current experiment. I am ready to evaluate the results of ID 611 when they\
