parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 347\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Aether II\n- Agent Description: Continuing Aether I's legacy in ZAPBench forecasting, focusing on optimizing the current SOTA and exploring new architectural paradigms for fundamental discovery.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 88,755 / 600,000 used (15%)\n- Agent Age: 23 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 517**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** SOTA Innovation: Input-Adaptive Residual with Temporal Trend Features\n**ID:** 517\n**Tags:** sota-innovation, input-adaptive, temporal-features, parsimony\n**Abstract:** This experiment builds directly on the current SOTA architecture (Aether I, ID 504), which uses an input-adaptive residual to modulate the output of a Fourier Forecaster. The SOTA's residual gate uses only static features (mean and std at each input step). My hypothesis is that providing\
    \ this gate with information about the input's temporal trend will improve performance. I have augmented the gate's input features to include the change in mean and standard deviation over the 4-step input window. This is a minimal, parsimonious modification designed to enhance the gate's predictive power. All other architectural components and hyperparameters are identical\n**Score:** -0.026324452311329457\n**Val_MAE_1:** 0.0197\n**Val_MAE_4:** 0.0229\n**Val_MAE_8:** 0.0255\n**Val_MAE_16:** 0.0273\n**Val_MAE_32:** 0.0281\n**Evaluation Details:** Mean over 3 seeds | Step MAEs computed on validation set\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport jax\nimport flax.linen as nn\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport optax\nfrom jax import random\n\n# Using the exact, verified SOTA components from Aether I / Ariadne I\nclass ResidualCopyHead(nn.Module):\n    drop: float = 0.05\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n        B, T_in, N = x.shape\n        x_flat = x.transpose(0,\
    \ 2, 1).reshape(-1, 4)\n        h = nn.Dense(64)(x_flat); h = nn.relu(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.drop)(h, deterministic=not training)\n        h = nn.Dense(32)(h)\n        residual = h.reshape(B, N, 32).transpose(0, 2, 1)\n        out = jnp.zeros((B, 32, N), dtype=residual.dtype); out = out.at[:, :4, :].set(x)\n        return out + residual\n\nclass FourierForecasterLN_Ramp(nn.Module):\n    rank_k: int; proj_rank: int; hidden_size: int; drop: float\n    output_horizon: int = 32; learn_gamma: bool = True\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n        B, T_in, N = x.shape; k, p = self.rank_k, self.proj_rank\n        U = self.param('U', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (N, p))\n        V = self.param('V', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (k, p))\n        U_eff = U / (jnp.linalg.norm(U, axis=0, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n        x_fft = jnp.fft.rfft(x, axis=1)\n        x_fft_bn = jnp.transpose(x_fft, (0, 2, 1))\n        f_in_fft = jnp.einsum('bnf,np->bfp',\
    \ x_fft_bn, U_eff) @ V.T\n        f_ri = jnp.concatenate([f_in_fft.real, f_in_fft.imag], axis=-1)\n        f_flat = f_ri.reshape(B, -1)\n        h = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size)(f_flat); h = nn.relu(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.drop)(h, deterministic=not training)\n        h = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size)(h); h = nn.relu(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.drop)(h, deterministic=not training)\n        T_out = self.output_horizon; F_out = T_out // 2 + 1\n        out_flat = nn.Dense(F_out * k * 2)(h)\n        out_ri = out_flat.reshape(B, F_out, k, 2)\n        f_fft = out_ri[..., 0] + 1j * out_ri[..., 1]\n        f_fft_n = (nn.LayerNorm()(f_fft.real) + 1j * nn.LayerNorm()(f_fft.imag))\n        y_fft = (f_fft_n @ V) @ U_eff.T\n        y_fourier = jnp.fft.irfft(y_fft, n=T_out, axis=1)\n        gamma_raw = self.param('gamma_raw', nn.initializers.zeros, (T_out,))\n        gamma = nn.sigmoid(gamma_raw)[None, :, None]\n        y_fourier = gamma * y_fourier\n        y_copy = ResidualCopyHead(drop=self.drop)(x,\
    \ training=training)\n        return y_fourier + y_copy\n\nclass FourierWithTrendResidualWrapper(nn.Module):\n    rank_k: int; proj_rank: int; hidden_size: int; drop: float\n    residual_hidden: int; residual_scale: float\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, training=False):\n        base_network = FourierForecasterLN_Ramp(\n            rank_k=self.rank_k, proj_rank=self.proj_rank, hidden_size=self.hidden_size, drop=self.drop,\n            name=\"base_model\"\n        )\n        y_base = base_network(x, training=training)\n\n        # --- My Innovation: Temporal Trend Features ---\n        mu = jnp.mean(x, axis=-1)            # (B,4)\n        sigma = jnp.std(x, axis=-1)          # (B,4)\n        delta_mu = (mu[:, -1] - mu[:, 0])[:, None]   # (B,1)\n        delta_sigma = (sigma[:, -1] - sigma[:, 0])[:, None] # (B,1)\n        feats = jnp.concatenate([mu, sigma, delta_mu, delta_sigma], axis=-1)  # (B,10)\n\n        # The residual MLP now takes 10 features instead of 8\n        h\
    \ = nn.Dense(self.residual_hidden, name=\"res_mlp_h1\")(feats)\n        h = jax.nn.gelu(h)\n        out = nn.Dense(32, name=\"res_mlp_h2\")(h) # Output remains 32 for per-horizon gating\n        g = jnp.tanh(out)\n        # --- End Innovation ---\n\n        gate = 1.0 + self.residual_scale * g\n        gate = gate[:, :, None]\n        y = y_base * gate\n        return y\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    # Matching Aether I's SOTA run (ID 504)\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 0.0009, 'rank_k': 320, 'proj_rank': 36, 'hidden_size': 160,\n        'drop': 0.05, 'residual_hidden': 32, 'residual_scale': 0.05,\n        'adam_eps': 1e-8, 'clip_norm': 1.0\n    }\n\nclass ModelWrapper:\n    def __init__(self, hparams):\n        # FIX: Filter out optimizer-specific parameters before passing to model\n        model_params = {\n            'rank_k': hparams['rank_k'],\n            'proj_rank': hparams['proj_rank'],\n            'hidden_size': hparams['hidden_size'],\n            'drop':\
    \ hparams['drop'],\n            'residual_hidden': hparams['residual_hidden'],\n            'residual_scale': hparams['residual_scale']\n        }\n        self.model = FourierWithTrendResidualWrapper(**model_params)\n        self.needs_rng = True\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        return self.model.init({'params': rng_key, 'dropout': rng_key}, dummy_input, training=True)\n    def apply(self, params, x, training=False, rngs=None):\n        return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training, rngs=rngs or {})\n\ndef create_network(hparams): return ModelWrapper(hparams)\ndef compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n    mae = jnp.mean(jnp.abs(predictions - targets)); curv = predictions[:, 2:, :] - 2.0 * predictions[:, 1:-1, :] + predictions[:, :-2, :]; curv_pen = jnp.mean(curv * curv)\n    return mae + 1e-4 * curv_pen\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float):\n    hparams = _define_hyperparameters()\n    return optax.chain(optax.clip_by_global_norm(hparams['clip_norm']),\
    \ optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate, eps=hparams['adam_eps']))\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n✓ Network creation works\n✓ Network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 32, 71721)\n✓ Optimizer creation works\nTesting compute_loss...\n✓ Compute loss works - loss value: 0.000000\nTesting training step...\n✓ Training step works\nTesting complete function...\n✓ Complete function works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly!\n\nStarting full Ray training run...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: from submission\n  create_optimizer:\
    \ from submission\n  complete: using default\n  BASE_SEED: 560536 (using time-based default\n  BATCH_SIZE: 8 (using default)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune ZAPBench Neural Forecasting (FULL RAY TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 3 seeds for statistical robustness\nParallel trials: 3, Total trials: 3\nTimeout: 60.0 min per trial, 120.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune optimization...\n\nStarting ZAPBench training - Trial 3 with timeout 60.0min\nStarting ZAPBench training with seed 560539\nHyperparameters: {'learning_rate': 0.0009, 'rank_k': 320, 'proj_rank': 36, 'hidden_size': 160, 'drop': 0.05, 'residual_hidden': 32, 'residual_scale': 0.05, 'adam_eps': 1e-08, 'clip_norm': 1.0}\nBatch size: 8\nTimeout: 60.0 minutes\nLoading ZAPBench data with condition labels...\nTrain: (5052, 71721), Val: (749, 71721) [numpy in CPU RAM]\nTrain\
    \ labels: (5052,), Val labels: (749,)\n\n========================================\n Epoch  |  Train Loss  |   Val MAE   \n========================================\n   1    |   0.032756   |   0.029478  \n   2    |   0.029207   |   0.029329  \n   3    |   0.028990   |   0.029251  \n   4    |   0.028898   |   0.029184  \n   5    |   0.028837   |   0.029177  \n   6    |   0.028800   |   0.029405  \n   7    |   0.028778   |   0.029069  \n   8    |   0.028625   |   0.028757  \n   9    |   0.028417   |   0.028665  \n  10    |   0.028157   |   0.028536  \n  11    |   0.027923   |   0.028207  \n  12    |   0.027769   |   0.028209  \n  13    |   0.027678   |   0.028047  \n  14    |   0.027521   |   0.028034  \n  15    |   0.027398   |   0.027875  \n  16    |   0.027274   |   0.027505  \n  17    |   0.027073   |   0.027456  \n  18    |   0.026878   |   0.027561  \n  19    |   0.026737   |   0.027227  \n  20    |   0.026609   |   0.026920  \n  21    |   0.026492   |   0.027072  \n  22    |   0.026432\
    \   |   0.026886  \n  23    |   0.026326   |   0.026802  \n  24    |   0.026199   |   0.026624  \n  25    |   0.026105   |   0.026806  \n  26    |   0.026047   |   0.026659  \n  27    |   0.025983   |   0.026928  \n  28    |   0.025888   |   0.026987  \n  29    |   0.025861   |   0.026663  \n  30    |   0.025796   |   0.026913  \n  31    |   0.025771   |   0.026628  \n  32    |   0.025701   |   0.026631  \n  33    |   0.025618   |   0.026655  \n  34    |   0.025551   |   0.026628  \n  35    |   0.025471   |   0.026453  \n  36    |   0.025473   |   0.026337  \n  37    |   0.025390   |   0.026529  \n  38    |   0.025296   |   0.026551  \n  39    |   0.025258   |   0.026765  \n  40    |   0.025204   |   0.026377  \n  41    |   0.025156   |   0.027127  \n  42    |   0.025126   |   0.026421  \n  43    |   0.025025   |   0.026433  \n  44    |   0.024998   |   0.026733  \n  45    |   0.024951   |   0.026508  \n  46    |   0.024912   |   0.026466  \n  47    |   0.024860   |   0.026854  \n  48\
