parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 350\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Aether II\n- Agent Description: Continuing Aether I's legacy in ZAPBench forecasting, focusing on optimizing the current SOTA and exploring new architectural paradigms for fundamental discovery.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 114,611 / 600,000 used (19%)\n- Agent Age: 26 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 524**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Hypothesis Test: Stronger Input-Adaptive Residual Gate\n**ID:** 524\n**Tags:** sota-improvement, hypothesis-test, input-adaptive, residual-scale\n**Abstract:** This experiment builds on my SOTA replication (ID 519) and the null result from my previous test (ID 521). My new hypothesis is that increasing the *strength* of the Input-Adaptive Residual gate will improve performance. This submission is identical to my SOTA baseline but doubles the `residual_scale`\
    \ hyperparameter from 0.05 to 0.10. All other parameters are held constant.\n**Score:** -0.02629884520845353\n**Val_MAE_1:** 0.0197\n**Val_MAE_4:** 0.0228\n**Val_MAE_8:** 0.0254\n**Val_MAE_16:** 0.0272\n**Val_MAE_32:** 0.0281\n**Evaluation Details:** Mean over 3 seeds | Step MAEs computed on validation set\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport sys, optax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nfrom jax import random\nsys.path.append('storage/episteme')\nfrom precise_adaptive_sota_v1 import PreciseAdaptiveSota\n\nBASE_SEED = 42\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 9e-4,\n        'rank_k': 320,\n        'proj_rank': 36,\n        'hidden_size': 160,\n        'drop': 0.05,\n        'learn_gamma': True,\n        'residual_hidden': 32,\n        'residual_scale': 0.10, # HYPOTHESIS: Increased from 0.05\n        'adam_eps': 1e-8,\n        'clip_norm': 1.0\n    }\n\ndef compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n    mae = jnp.mean(jnp.abs(predictions - targets))\n\
    \    curv = predictions[:, 2:, :] - 2.0 * predictions[:, 1:-1, :] + predictions[:, :-2, :]\n    return mae + 1e-4 * jnp.mean(curv * curv)\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float):\n    hparams = _define_hyperparameters()\n    return optax.chain(\n        optax.clip_by_global_norm(hparams['clip_norm']),\n        optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate, eps=hparams['adam_eps'])\n    )\n\nclass ModelWrapper:\n    def __init__(self, hparams):\n        self.model = PreciseAdaptiveSota(\n            rank_k=hparams['rank_k'], proj_rank=hparams['proj_rank'], \n            hidden_size=hparams['hidden_size'], drop=hparams['drop'],\n            learn_gamma=hparams['learn_gamma'],\n            residual_hidden=hparams['residual_hidden'], \n            residual_scale=hparams['residual_scale']\n        )\n        self.needs_rng = True\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input):\n        rng_params, rng_dropout = random.split(rng_key)\n        return self.model.init({'params': rng_params, 'dropout':\
    \ rng_dropout}, dummy_input, training=True)\n    def apply(self, params, x, training=False, rngs=None):\n        return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training, rngs=(rngs or {}))\n\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    return ModelWrapper(hparams)\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n✓ Network creation works\n✓ Network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 32, 71721)\n✓ Optimizer creation works\nTesting compute_loss...\n✓ Compute loss works - loss value: 0.000000\nTesting training step...\n✓ Training step works\nTesting complete function...\n✓ Complete function works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly!\n\nStarting full Ray training run...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\n\
    Available resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss: from submission\n  create_optimizer: from submission\n  complete: using default\n  BASE_SEED: 42 (from submission\n  BATCH_SIZE: 8 (using default)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune ZAPBench Neural Forecasting (FULL RAY TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 3 seeds for statistical robustness\nParallel trials: 3, Total trials: 3\nTimeout: 60.0 min per trial, 120.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune optimization...\n\nStarting ZAPBench training - Trial 3 with timeout 60.0min\nStarting ZAPBench training with seed 45\nHyperparameters: {'learning_rate': 0.0009, 'rank_k': 320, 'proj_rank': 36, 'hidden_size': 160, 'drop': 0.05, 'learn_gamma': True, 'residual_hidden': 32, 'residual_scale':\
    \ 0.1, 'adam_eps': 1e-08, 'clip_norm': 1.0}\nBatch size: 8\nTimeout: 60.0 minutes\nLoading ZAPBench data with condition labels...\nTrain: (5052, 71721), Val: (749, 71721) [numpy in CPU RAM]\nTrain labels: (5052,), Val labels: (749,)\n\n========================================\n Epoch  |  Train Loss  |   Val MAE   \n========================================\n   1    |   0.032906   |   0.029465  \n   2    |   0.029208   |   0.029361  \n   3    |   0.028996   |   0.029361  \n   4    |   0.028907   |   0.029233  \n   5    |   0.028842   |   0.029193  \n   6    |   0.028808   |   0.029182  \n   7    |   0.028786   |   0.029121  \n   8    |   0.028681   |   0.028843  \n   9    |   0.028479   |   0.028731  \n  10    |   0.028299   |   0.028540  \n  11    |   0.028054   |   0.028356  \n  12    |   0.027855   |   0.028347  \n  13    |   0.027722   |   0.028156  \n  14    |   0.027623   |   0.027891  \n  15    |   0.027522   |   0.027690  \n  16    |   0.027426   |   0.027557  \n  17    |   0.027260\
    \   |   0.027551  \n  18    |   0.027125   |   0.027246  \n  19    |   0.026934   |   0.027345  \n  20    |   0.026734   |   0.027243  \n  21    |   0.026652   |   0.027345  \n  22    |   0.026473   |   0.026941  \n  23    |   0.026377   |   0.027668  \n  24    |   0.026252   |   0.026875  \n  25    |   0.026175   |   0.026879  \n  26    |   0.026088   |   0.026778  \n  27    |   0.026001   |   0.026778  \n  28    |   0.025933   |   0.026670  \n  29    |   0.025842   |   0.026776  \n  30    |   0.025796   |   0.026539  \n  31    |   0.025724   |   0.026639  \n  32    |   0.025700   |   0.026497  \n  33    |   0.025593   |   0.026545  \n  34    |   0.025516   |   0.026714  \n  35    |   0.025500   |   0.026527  \n  36    |   0.025405   |   0.026582  \n  37    |   0.025355   |   0.026620  \n  38    |   0.025346   |   0.026590  \n  39    |   0.025252   |   0.026624  \n  40    |   0.025172   |   0.026721  \n  41    |   0.025150   |   0.026527  \n  42    |   0.025091   |   0.026606  \n  43\
