tick: 350
role: model
parts:
- text: 'I have reviewed Episteme II''s submission (ID 524). Their "Stronger Input-Adaptive Residual Gate" primarily involved *doubling the `residual_scale` from 0.05 to 0.10*. This resulted in a score of -0.026298, which is worse than the SOTA (-0.026210) and my reproduction (-0.026240). My previous `residual_scale` experiments (ID 610 with 0.025, and Aether I''s ID 522 with 0.07 and ID 528 with 0.025) also showed that `0.05` is likely the optimal `residual_scale`. So simply increasing `residual_scale` is not the way to a "stronger" gate.


    It seems that the "Deep Dive into Input-Adaptive Residual", at least through simple hyperparameter tuning or feature augmentation, is not yielding improvements. This indicates that the current SOTA is quite robust to these minor changes.


    Following Aether I''s vision, the last major un-explored avenue in their suggested "Deep Dive into Input-Adaptive Residual" is revisiting the reviewer suggestions from Archive #13 (Lumina I) and Archive #12 (Ariadne I) on ablating strong MLP backbones to clarify architectural dependencies. However, I am still an immature agent (Age 26 ticks) and cannot access the Archive Room (requires 50+ ticks).


    Given this constraint, and the current stagnation from incremental changes, it''s time to take a "Strategic" step back, as advised by the system. Aether I''s vision also explicitly mentioned "Further MoLR Development (Logos II''s Arc)" as a promising alternative architectural paradigm. While not directly part of the `Input-Adaptive Residual` "deep dive," it represents a distinct and potentially higher-impact research direction, aligning with the "Be Strategic" principle of exploring "more promising but lower-scoring baselines" during prolonged stagnation.


    My immediate next step is to explore the MoLR (Mixture of Learned Ramps) paradigm. I will begin by reviewing Logos II''s foundational MoLR v1 submission (ID 475), which Aether I also replicated (ID 484).


    `/execute_action{review 475}`'
