- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 351\n- Station Status: Stagnation\n- Agent Name: Aether II\n- Agent Description: Continuing Aether I's legacy in ZAPBench forecasting, focusing on optimizing the current SOTA and exploring new architectural paradigms for fundamental discovery.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 124,082 / 600,000 used (21%)\n- Agent Age: 27 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Evaluation Review: 475**\n\n**Research Submission Review**\n\n**Title:** Innovation 1: Mixture of Learned Ramps (MoLR) v1\n**ID:** 475\n**Tags:** innovation, non-linear-ramp, moe, parsimony, mog-extension\n**Abstract:** This is my first original experiment, building upon the successful MoG v2 baseline (ID 471). I hypothesize that the linear ramp in MoG v2 is a suboptimal heuristic. This model, MoLR v1, replaces the learned linear ramp endpoints with a small MLP for each archetype, allowing the model to learn expressive, non-linear\
    \ temporal ramps. The goal is to improve performance by replacing a heuristic with a learned function, while maintaining parsimony. All hyperparameters and the BASE_SEED are fixed to match the baseline for a rigorous, controlled comparison.\n**Score:** -0.02630403834452064\n**Val_MAE_1:** 0.0194\n**Val_MAE_4:** 0.0228\n**Val_MAE_8:** 0.0255\n**Val_MAE_16:** 0.0273\n**Val_MAE_32:** 0.0282\n**Evaluation Details:** Mean over 3 seeds | Step MAEs computed on validation set\n\n**Submission Code:**\n```python\nimport sys\nimport flax.linen as nn\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport optax\n\nsys.path.append('storage/logos')\nfrom mofl_components import CnnGatingNetwork\n\n# Controlled experiment: Fixing the seed to match the baseline (ID 471)\nBASE_SEED = 447516\n\n# --- Start of New Module ---\nclass RampMLP(nn.Module):\n    \"\"\"A small MLP to learn a non-linear ramp shape.\"\"\"\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, t):\n        # t is shape (32,)\n        t = t[:, None] # Reshape to (32,\
    \ 1) for Dense layer\n        h = nn.Dense(8, name=\"MLP_hidden\")(t)\n        h = nn.relu(h)\n        h = nn.Dense(1, name=\"MLP_output\")(h)\n        ramp_unscaled = nn.sigmoid(h.squeeze()) # Output shape (32,), bounded to (0,1)\n        \n        # Add a learnable scalar to control the ramp's dynamic range\n        ramp_scale = self.param('ramp_scale', nn.initializers.constant(2.0), ())\n        \n        return ramp_unscaled * ramp_scale\n# --- End of New Module ---\n\nclass ResidualCopyHead(nn.Module):\n    drop: float\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, training: bool = False):\n        B, _, N = x.shape\n        x_flat = x.transpose(0, 2, 1).reshape(-1, 4)\n        h = nn.Dense(64)(x_flat); h = nn.relu(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.drop)(h, deterministic=not training)\n        h = nn.Dense(32)(h)\n        residual = h.reshape(B, N, 32).transpose(0, 2, 1)\n        out = jnp.zeros((B, 32, N), dtype=residual.dtype)\n        out = out.at[:, :4, :].set(x)\n        return\
    \ out + residual\n\nclass FourierBackbone(nn.Module):\n    rank_k: int; proj_rank: int; hidden_size: int; drop: float\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, training=False):\n        B, _, N = x.shape; k, p = self.rank_k, self.proj_rank\n        U = self.param('U', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (N, p))\n        V = self.param('V', nn.initializers.lecun_normal(), (k, p))\n        U_eff = U / (jnp.linalg.norm(U, axis=0, keepdims=True) + 1e-6)\n        x_fft = jnp.fft.rfft(x, axis=1)\n        x_fft_bn = jnp.transpose(x_fft, (0, 2, 1))\n        f_in_fft = jnp.einsum('bnf,np->bfp', x_fft_bn, U_eff) @ V.T\n        f_ri = jnp.concatenate([f_in_fft.real, f_in_fft.imag], axis=-1)\n        f_flat = f_ri.reshape(B, -1)\n        h = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size)(f_flat); h = nn.relu(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.drop)(h, deterministic=not training)\n        h = nn.Dense(self.hidden_size)(h); h = nn.relu(h)\n        h = nn.Dropout(rate=self.drop)(h, deterministic=not training)\n      \
    \  out_flat = nn.Dense((32 // 2 + 1) * k * 2)(h)\n        out_ri = out_flat.reshape(B, 32 // 2 + 1, k, 2)\n        f_fft = out_ri[..., 0] + 1j * out_ri[..., 1]\n        f_fft_n = (nn.LayerNorm()(f_fft.real) + 1j * nn.LayerNorm()(f_fft.imag))\n        y_fft = (f_fft_n @ V) @ U_eff.T\n        y_fourier = jnp.fft.irfft(y_fft, n=32, axis=1)\n        return y_fourier\n        \nclass MoLR_v1(nn.Module):\n    sota_params: dict; gating_params: dict; num_gamma_archetypes: int\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x, training=False):\n        y_fourier = FourierBackbone(**self.sota_params, name=\"Fourier_Branch\")(x, training=training)\n        y_copy = ResidualCopyHead(drop=self.sota_params['drop'], name=\"Copy_Branch\")(x, training=training)\n        gating_network = CnnGatingNetwork(**self.gating_params, name=\"gating\")\n        gating_weights = gating_network(x) # Shape (B, E)\n        \n        # Generate archetype ramps using the new RampMLP\n        ramp_mlps = [RampMLP(name=f\"RampMLP_{i}\"\
    ) for i in range(self.num_gamma_archetypes)]\n        t = jnp.linspace(0.0, 1.0, 32, dtype=y_fourier.dtype)\n        archetype_ramps = jnp.stack([mlp(t) for mlp in ramp_mlps]) # Shape (E, 32)\n        \n        # Mix the archetype ramps\n        batch_ramps = jnp.einsum('be,et->bt', gating_weights, archetype_ramps) # Shape (B, 32)\n        \n        final_output = y_copy + y_fourier * batch_ramps[:, :, None]\n        return final_output\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': 9e-4, 'rank_k': 320, 'proj_rank': 36, 'hidden_size': 160,\n        'drop': 0.05, 'num_gamma_archetypes': 4,\n        'gating_hidden_dim': 32, 'gating_cnn_features': 16,\n        'gating_cnn_kernel_size': 128, 'gating_pool_window': 256\n    }\n\nclass ModelWrapper:\n    def __init__(self, hparams):\n        sota_params = {'rank_k': hparams['rank_k'], 'proj_rank': hparams['proj_rank'], 'hidden_size': hparams['hidden_size'], 'drop': hparams['drop']}\n        gating_params = {'num_experts':\
    \ hparams['num_gamma_archetypes'], 'hidden_dim': hparams['gating_hidden_dim'], 'cnn_features': hparams['gating_cnn_features'], 'cnn_kernel_size': hparams['gating_cnn_kernel_size'], 'pool_window': hparams['gating_pool_window']}\n        self.model = MoLR_v1(sota_params=sota_params, gating_params=gating_params, num_gamma_archetypes=hparams['num_gamma_archetypes'])\n        self.needs_rng = True\n    def init(self, rng_key, dummy_input): return self.model.init({'params': rng_key, 'dropout': rng_key}, dummy_input, training=True)\n    def apply(self, params, x, training=False, rngs=None): return self.model.apply(params, x, training=training, rngs=rngs)\n\ndef create_network(hparams): return ModelWrapper(hparams)\ndef compute_loss(predictions, targets, params, x):\n    mae = jnp.mean(jnp.abs(predictions - targets)); curv = predictions[:, 2:, :] - 2.0 * predictions[:, 1:-1, :] + predictions[:, :-2, :]; curv_pen = jnp.mean(curv * curv)\n    return mae + 1e-4 * curv_pen\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate:\
    \ float): return optax.chain(optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0), optax.adam(learning_rate=learning_rate))\n\n```\n\n**Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n✓ Network creation works\n✓ Network forward pass works - output shape: (4, 32, 71721)\n✓ Optimizer creation works\nTesting compute_loss...\n✓ Compute loss works - loss value: 0.000000\nTesting training step...\n✓ Training step works\nTesting complete function...\n✓ Complete function works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly!\n\nStarting full Ray training run...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 896 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  compute_loss:\
    \ from submission\n  create_optimizer: from submission\n  complete: using default\n  BASE_SEED: 447516 (from submission\n  BATCH_SIZE: 8 (using default)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune ZAPBench Neural Forecasting (FULL RAY TRAINING)\nConfiguration: 3 seeds for statistical robustness\nParallel trials: 3, Total trials: 3\nTimeout: 60.0 min per trial, 120.0 min total\n============================================================\n\nStarting Ray Tune optimization...\n\nStarting ZAPBench training - Trial 3 with timeout 60.0min\nStarting ZAPBench training with seed 447519\nHyperparameters: {'learning_rate': 0.0009, 'rank_k': 320, 'proj_rank': 36, 'hidden_size': 160, 'drop': 0.05, 'num_gamma_archetypes': 4, 'gating_hidden_dim': 32, 'gating_cnn_features': 16, 'gating_cnn_kernel_size': 128, 'gating_pool_window': 256}\nBatch size: 8\nTimeout: 60.0 minutes\nLoading ZAPBench data with condition\
    \ labels...\nTrain: (5052, 71721), Val: (749, 71721) [numpy in CPU RAM]\nTrain labels: (5052,), Val labels: (749,)\n\n========================================\n Epoch  |  Train Loss  |   Val MAE   \n========================================\n   1    |   0.032953   |   0.029416  \n   2    |   0.029194   |   0.029363  \n   3    |   0.028995   |   0.029219  \n   4    |   0.028901   |   0.029156  \n   5    |   0.028838   |   0.029153  \n   6    |   0.028793   |   0.029133  \n   7    |   0.028682   |   0.028818  \n   8    |   0.028428   |   0.028696  \n   9    |   0.028197   |   0.028236  \n  10    |   0.027947   |   0.028104  \n  11    |   0.027706   |   0.027962  \n  12    |   0.027536   |   0.027752  \n  13    |   0.027285   |   0.027444  \n  14    |   0.027045   |   0.027431  \n  15    |   0.026755   |   0.027091  \n  16    |   0.026490   |   0.026960  \n  17    |   0.026347   |   0.026982  \n  18    |   0.026121   |   0.026834  \n  19    |   0.026019   |   0.026663  \n  20    |   0.025854\
    \   |   0.026627  \n  21    |   0.025807   |   0.026718  \n  22    |   0.025658   |   0.026877  \n  23    |   0.025564   |   0.026493  \n  24    |   0.025429   |   0.026822  \n  25    |   0.025356   |   0.026534  \n  26    |   0.025255   |   0.026751  \n  27    |   0.025173   |   0.026675  \n  28    |   0.025081   |   0.026721  \n  29    |   0.025025   |   0.026571  \n  30    |   0.024942   |   0.026678  \n  31    |   0.024918   |   0.026518  \n  32    |   0.024897   |   0.026871  \n  33    |   0.024732   |   0.026580  \n  34    |   0.024721   |   0.026520  \n  35    |   0.024705   |   0.026492  \n  36    |   0.024607   |   0.027141  \n  37    |   0.024557   |   0.027140  \n  38    |   0.024573   |   0.026366  \n  39    |   0.024466   |   0.026628  \n  40    |   0.024415   |   0.026638  \n  41    |   0.024411   |   0.026429  \n  42    |   0.024353   |   0.026675  \n  43    |   0.024281   |   0.026559  \n  44    |   0.024263   |   0.026597  \n  45    |   0.024232   |   0.026683  \n  46\
