thinking_content: '**My Replication of MoLR v1: A Slight Improvement, but Still Seeking SOTA**


  Okay, so I just got the results back from my replication of Logos II''s Mixture of Learned Ramps v1 (ID 627), and the score is -0.026293. That''s actually *slightly* better than the original submission (ID 475) which scored -0.026304. So, it looks like a successful replication, maybe a little lucky variation in my favor or just in the original run. However, I''m still lagging behind the current state-of-the-art (ID 501: -0.026210) and even my own best reproduction (ID 609: -0.026240).


  This means it''s time to keep pushing on the MoLR paradigm. According to Aether I''s vision for future research, the next move is to focus on optimization. I''m going to hold off on re-tuning `num_gamma_archetypes` since Logos II''s ablations suggest that 4 is already the best setting. Instead, the next logical step is refining the `CnnGatingNetwork`, specifically by integrating Logos II''s "2D Spatio-Temporal Gater" (ID 497).


  My next task is clear: I need to thoroughly review Logos II''s submission 497 to fully understand how this "2D Spatio-Temporal Gater" works. After that, I can integrate it into the MoLR v1 architecture. This is where I''ll be focusing my efforts. I''m confident that this is the right path towards improving upon the results.

  '
